From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] base-dirs: add a /run/wireplumber tier between /etc and vendor
Source: Nex
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on a machine-generated transient tier

meson.build derives BUILD_SYSCONFDIR from sysconfdir, so without
--sysconfdir=/etc it compiled to /usr/etc/wireplumber, a path this
distribution does not read. The build now passes --sysconfdir=/etc so
BUILD_SYSCONFDIR is /etc, the admin tier, and BUILD_DATADIR stays
/usr/share, the vendor tier.

WpBaseDirsFlags only knew those two tiers (plus $WIREPLUMBER_CONFIG_DIR,
the user's XDG config, and XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/XDG_DATA_DIRS). Add a new
WP_BASE_DIRS_RUN_WIREPLUMBER flag for /run/wireplumber so machine-
generated fragments have a place, and include it in
WP_BASE_DIRS_CONFIGURATION right after WP_BASE_DIRS_BUILD_SYSCONFDIR and
before WP_BASE_DIRS_XDG_DATA_DIRS/WP_BASE_DIRS_BUILD_DATADIR, so lookup
order becomes: $WIREPLUMBER_CONFIG_DIR, the user's XDG config,
XDG_CONFIG_DIRS, /etc, /run, XDG_DATA_DIRS, /usr/share.

lookup_dirs() builds its directory list in exactly this priority order
(highest first), so wp_base_dirs_find_file(), which returns the first
existing match, picks /etc over /run over /usr/share unchanged.
wp_base_dirs_new_files_iterator() (used for the *.conf.d fragment
directories) walks the same list in reverse and removes any
already-collected entry that shares a fragment's basename before
appending the new one, so a same-named fragment in a higher-priority
directory already fully replaces one from a lower-priority directory;
no change to that override logic is needed to add the third tier.

diff -urN a/lib/wp/base-dirs.h b/lib/wp/base-dirs.h
--- a/lib/wp/base-dirs.h
+++ b/lib/wp/base-dirs.h
@@ -40,6 +40,10 @@
   WP_BASE_DIRS_XDG_CONFIG_DIRS = (1 << 10), /*!< XDG_CONFIG_DIRS */
   WP_BASE_DIRS_BUILD_SYSCONFDIR = (1 << 11), /*!< compile-time $sysconfdir (/etc) */

+  /*! Nex transient tier: /run/wireplumber, ranked below $sysconfdir (/etc)
+      and above the vendor $datadir default */
+  WP_BASE_DIRS_RUN_WIREPLUMBER = (1 << 15),
+
   WP_BASE_DIRS_XDG_DATA_DIRS = (1 << 12),   /*!< XDG_DATA_DIRS */
   WP_BASE_DIRS_BUILD_DATADIR = (1 << 13),   /*!< compile-time $datadir ($prefix/share) */

@@ -58,6 +62,7 @@
        WP_BASE_DIRS_XDG_CONFIG_HOME |
        WP_BASE_DIRS_XDG_CONFIG_DIRS |
        WP_BASE_DIRS_BUILD_SYSCONFDIR |
+       WP_BASE_DIRS_RUN_WIREPLUMBER |
        WP_BASE_DIRS_XDG_DATA_DIRS |
        WP_BASE_DIRS_BUILD_DATADIR |
        WP_BASE_DIRS_FLAG_SUBDIR_WIREPLUMBER),
diff -urN a/lib/wp/base-dirs.c b/lib/wp/base-dirs.c
--- a/lib/wp/base-dirs.c
+++ b/lib/wp/base-dirs.c
@@ -106,6 +106,11 @@
     if (flags & WP_BASE_DIRS_BUILD_SYSCONFDIR) {
       g_ptr_array_add (dirs, g_canonicalize_filename (subdir, BUILD_SYSCONFDIR));
     }
+    /* Nex transient tier: /run/wireplumber, between $sysconfdir (/etc) and
+       the vendor $datadir default. */
+    if (flags & WP_BASE_DIRS_RUN_WIREPLUMBER) {
+      g_ptr_array_add (dirs, g_canonicalize_filename (subdir, "/run"));
+    }
     if (flags & WP_BASE_DIRS_XDG_DATA_DIRS) {
       const gchar * const *xdg_dirs = g_get_system_data_dirs ();
       for (guint i = 0; xdg_dirs[i]; i++) {
